  "assumptions": [
    "Existing accepted algorithms, code/resource/stack/provider domains unchanged; no theorem is widened",
    "Both physical records always exist. Fixed positions, simulation pixels, draw caches/history, animation, platform, carried/destination/fare/minimum-fare and each command word are independent retained raw16-bit patterns",
    "Two-word physical arrays map into two native player records via an explicit stride; unusual raw byte indices retain physical cross-field aliases, not invented third-player storage",
    "Interleaved HUD icon caches2800..2803 remain presentation-owned. Cycle starts0CFA/0CFC and ends0CFC/0CFE share one existing resource word; impact limits remain resource views. No model writer is not a constness proof; foreign byte windows still preserve mutations",
    "Cold import is verification fixture initialization only; live moved RAM stays sealed and serializers write only the separate observation view",
    "Callbacks/service replies are synchronous under the accepted scheduler. Live reply and post-stone mutation evidence is finite; no new asynchronous delivery or backend policy",
    "Atomic ICE has equal returned RAM/ports; internal backwards decode versus ascending completed-buffer publication is not a write-instruction stream contract"
  ],
